Catch-all ghost pages: live serves the home HTML shell (141,355 B) for ANY unknown path incl. /#n, /gcp-app/home/, and the /blogs/token-refresh-... slug. Those are replicated as captured (mirror holds the same shell at the same paths — parity with live behavior, matching the D29 /contact/ ghost lesson in reverse: here the ghost IS the only thing live returns, so it's faithful).

Ghost-cache audit (D29 rule): home/developers/integrations/contact/blog spot-checked live-fetch size vs vendored — all within the expected delta of URL-rewrite length (141355 vs 141607 = absolute->relative src/href shortening, verified by byte diff: only asset-path rewrites differ); no stale-build pollution survived the crawl. Live serves a stable 141,355 B home on repeated fetches.
